{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:daac0c8586d69567","name":"Kintan Strider","source":{"id":"source:reference-daac0c8586d69567","title":"Kintan Strider","revision":18947,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T21:01:27Z","sha256":"90d27b59f5e30d6bd9a6499aaa9f6db2d5fcd8a5734156d385b02e148b58f631","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=18947","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Kintan%20Strider&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-daac0c8586d69567","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Threats of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Threats_of_the_Galaxy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Now extinct on its home planet, the Kintan Strider can be found on various other planets of the galaxy, where it is used as a guard beast by ",{"tag":"a","children":["Hutt Crime Lords"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hutt_Crime_Lords"}," or as an opponent in gladiatorial combat in less civilized societies. Kintan Striders are enormous beasts with huge shoulders and arms that nearly drag on the ground. A Kintan Strider does not have a neck- its over exaggerated face sits squarely in the middle of its chest, protected by a thick layer of fat and hide.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Although they are barely intelligent, Kintan Striders have learned how to use branches and poles as weapons, bashing their prey with powerful two-handed swings. Some even utilize these weapons to shovel food In their mouths, giving the appearance to uneducated observers that they are actually sentient, tool-using beings. Kintan Striders possess incredible healing abilities and can come back from wounds that would easily kill ",{"tag":"a","children":["Beasts"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Beasts"}," of similar size.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Although few citizens of the galaxy have ever seen a Kintan Strider, almost everyone knows the creature as a piece in the game called Dejarik and is familiar with its signature move, the Kintan Strider death gambit.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Kintan Strider Encounters"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Ironically, the one place this creature will never be encountered is the planet for which it is named. Millennia of hunting by the planet's primary species, the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nikto"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nikto","referenceId":"reference:0b47e2dd142a9955"},", nearly wiped out the Strider population. After the Hutts' domination of the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nikto"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nikto","referenceId":"reference:0b47e2dd142a9955"},", the few hundred surviving Striders were shipped offplanet, to be bred in captivity or released into the wilds on other, more hospitable worlds.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Heroes might run into a Kintan Strider within a crime lord's headquarters, where these creatures are kept as fodder for blood sports, or in \"execution pits\" where criminals are bludgeoned to death and eaten by these ravenous beasts. Crime lords who consider themselves notable Dejarik players sometimes mimic the game in real life, by utilizing the same types of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Beasts"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Beasts"}," found in the game within their collection of deadly creatures. True \"masters\" of this macabre game also employ the famous Kintan Strider death gambit, in which the Strider is sacrificed during the gladiatorial display in order for the victor to fall prey to some other creature kept in reserve.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Kintan Strider Statistics (CL 5)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Large ",{"tag":"a","children":["Beast"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Beast","referenceId":"reference:628bf77a740094a9"}," 6\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenc